From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:20:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 048/105] R2: GDN verify writes a/b straight into the
 RecoverSSM stash

SGLANG_GDN_AB_STASH_DIRECT=1 (default off).

gdn_mtp_cache_mode=none keeps a/b per GDN layer for accepted-state recovery.
The verify forward allocated fresh a/b, then copied both into the persistent
per-layer stash -- 2 device-to-device copies x 36 GDN layers = 72 small copies
per verify step. With the flag on, the layer asks the backend for the stash
slice before the projection and hands it to the producing kernel as the a/b
destination, so the values are stashed where they are produced.

- gdn_backend: `_fi_ab_stash` factors the (unchanged) allocate-or-return of the
  FlashInfer-recovery stash out of `forward_extend`; `gdn_ab_stash_out` returns
  `stash["a"][:B].view(B*T, H)` / same for b, but only for a FlashInfer-recovery
  target-verify -- decode, draft, draft_extend and prefill get None and keep
  allocating their own a/b. `forward_extend` skips each copy when the tensor it
  was handed already aliases the stash (data_ptr test, no host sync).
- triton_gdn_fused_proj: `fused_qkvzba_split_reshape_cat_contiguous` takes
  `out_a=`/`out_b=` so the existing split kernel stores into caller-owned
  buffers instead of fresh ones. Same stores, same values.
- qwen3_5 (inherited by qwen4_exp): asks the backend for the destinations and
  passes them down.

Buffer addresses are unchanged and still allocated once per layer, so the
recovery graphs captured by `capture_recovery_graphs` keep their pointers. The
write moves earlier inside the same verify forward; the next target forward
already joins on `_recovery_event` in `init_forward_metadata`, before any layer
runs, so the previous step's recovery cannot still be reading the stash.

Bit-exactness (real layer-0 weights, in_proj_qkv/z/a/b of
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-mtpft3, M=1/4/16): the stash contents written directly
by the split kernel are torch.equal to the a/b the unmodified path produces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
